{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions","id":1502203,"title":"Is it a good thing you can do Gay Death Rival Tragedy story in every Directions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-05T07:29:58-08:00","id":1502203,"title":"Is it a good thing you can do Gay Death Rival Tragedy story in every Directions?","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img width=\"2048\" height=\"2048\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1067161568200097893/1071723156928208936/IMG_3630.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1067161568200097893/1071723156928208936/IMG_3630.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1067161568200097893/1071723156928208936/IMG_3630.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> I assume that trans-directional games where the circle travels around the whole world are quite rare in Exalted and most campaigns just stay in a single area in one Direction, if it's true then does the directions written in a way that would be akin to one area but in four different layers of skin? So that every type of story can happen instead of pirate adventures being confided to the West or a tomb raiding requiring you to travel East? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T07:43:22-08:00","id":1502205,"title":"","content":"Hey Jen, I missed your posts!<br /> <br /> To some degree you're right. There's a lot of options in many of the directions. The West gets pirates, but the East gets River pirates, the South gets Sand Pirates (they sail on sandships) and then the North has Ice Pirates that sail ships on the ice. To some degree, almost any type of game idea can work in any direction, though some get changed a bit more than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T08:55:08-08:00","id":1502211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502205#post1502205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Jen, I missed your posts!<br /> <br /> To some degree you're right. There's a lot of options in many of the directions. The West gets pirates, but the East gets River pirates, the South gets Sand Pirates (they sail on sandships) and then the North has Ice Pirates that sail ships on the ice. To some degree, almost any type of game idea can work in any direction, though some get changed a bit more than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, it\u2019s mostly because I\u2019m thinking of writing a bunch of prose that explain why you wants to visit the four Directions, but since they are pretty much the same thing in different layer of skins and I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s a good or bad thing, like, going \u201cYou should spend your holiday in the South, we have all these amazing ruins that you can explore!\u201d feels weird when every other directions also has ruins &lt;-&lt;\u2018","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T11:04:35-08:00","id":1502223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502211#post1502211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yeah, it\u2019s mostly because I\u2019m thinking of writing a bunch of prose that explain why you wants to visit the four Directions, but since they are pretty much the same thing in different layer of skins and I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s a good or bad thing, like, going \u201cYou should spend your holiday in the South, we have all these amazing ruins that you can explore!\u201d feels weird when every other directions also has ruins &lt;-&lt;\u2018</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think the environment would matter a lot, that the experience of ruins in the middle of the desert is very different in apparent ways from one in the centre of a jungle. It's like, one of those is the episode of Avatar: The Last Airbender where they're fighting through a mysterious swamp, the other is where they've just lost Appa and have no shelter, no water, and no idea what direction to go in.<br /> <br /> If the Southern ruins are surrounding Chiaroscuro, you get the distinctions of interaction with the politics and culture of the Delzhan, both for their own distinctions and things like how control of water supplies is a focus of intrigue and competition, whereas in the East you're probably part of the complex subculture of people who raid these things and have a ready market for them like you're in an Indiana Jones knockoff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T05:15:55-08:00","id":1502379,"title":"","content":"I am currently running a game where my players will travel to all four directions (and then the Blessed Isle). This is their first time in Exalted and I wanted a game that gave them a bit of an intro to the way the world was set up, with the four directions, the Realm's satrapies and the various peoples and politics of creation. They started just south of the Riverlands, then headed South West by boat to Chiaroscuro and deeper into the desert. Now they are heading all the way North to Gethamane. After that its out to the Wavecrest Archipelago, then the Blessed Isle.<br /> The conceit (very simplified) is that they are a reborn group of solars who once ruled a great flying, teleporting city called the City of Golden Spires. They are searching for the control rods (effectively specialised hearthstones) that powered the city. Once they have all five they can find the city and raise it up again. The control rod/hearthstones are each located in manses aligned with the elemental poles. So theres a wood, fire, wind, water and earth manse, all dedicated to providing essence flow, via their hearthstones, to the city.<br /> Of course, the abyssals want the city too. The wyld hunt wants to kill the PCs AND the abyssals, the ancient spirit guardians of the manses aren't entirely convinced by the PCs, etc etc.<br /> <br /> Really the story lets me take the PCs to a whole bunch of exotic and fun places that are radically different to show that Creation is huge and very very varied. <br /> <br /> I have follow up campaigns that will focused more heavily on the underworld and the fae/wyld. But I'm holding off introducing either in the first game. Creation is enough to start with.<br /> <br /> And funnily enough, our pirate Dawn caste has already met the reincarnation of his lunar lover. Both of them are super manly macho bros and have become very close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T08:20:28-08:00","id":1502394,"title":"","content":"I imagine most ruins in Creation are going to have people living in or near them. Ruins are normally a good sign an area is at least viable for human habitation because someone stayed there long enough to build lasting structures.<br /> <br /> Obviously <i>normally</i> is the keyword here. First Age infrastructure and technology might have given them a different set of incentives for where they can put people and Exalts of any era have incentive to break ground in the middle of nowhere if the geomancy could yield a powerful manse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-07-2023, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T12:40:18-08:00","id":1502414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502394#post1502394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine most ruins in Creation are going to have people living in or near them. Ruins are normally a good sign an area is at least viable for human habitation because someone stayed there long enough to build lasting structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that can be considered a rule of thumb. A lot of places become reduced to ruins as a result of being abandoned for ages as a result of the area specifically <i>ceasing</i> to be fit for human habitation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T08:56:44-08:00","id":1502518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502414#post1502414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if that can be considered a rule of thumb. A lot of places become reduced to ruins as a result of being abandoned for ages as a result of the area specifically <i>ceasing</i> to be fit for human habitation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Environmentally linked settlement abandonments have historically been an outlier and I assume wyld zones and shadowlands wouldn't change that too drastically.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess if you're trying to factor the environmental impact of the Great Contagion killing 90% of all plant life, but I don't think that's being retained based on previous comments by developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-08-2023, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T12:35:07-08:00","id":1502531,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much the weird relation Creation has with its geography can play into that? Like the idea if a god dies or gets too lazy about something a river might start flowing differently until the gods notice enough to try to fix it. Course by the time Heaven finishes all their paperwork on the matter the new river might have new settlements with new gods vouching for keeping the river to its new course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T09:20:00-08:00","id":1502609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502518#post1502518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Environmentally linked settlement abandonments have historically been an outlier and I assume wyld zones and shadowlands wouldn't change that too drastically.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the premise where First Age buildings could have contained sorcery that is now broken and leaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T11:44:18-08:00","id":1502702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502211#post1502211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yeah, it\u2019s mostly because I\u2019m thinking of writing a bunch of prose that explain why you wants to visit the four Directions, but since they are pretty much the same thing in different layer of skins and I\u2019m wondering if that\u2019s a good or bad thing, like, going \u201cYou should spend your holiday in the South, we have all these amazing ruins that you can explore!\u201d feels weird when every other directions also has ruins &lt;-&lt;\u2018</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a trick.<br /> <br /> You can adapt <i>Macbeth</i> to feudal Japan (<i>Throne of Blood</i>), or <i>The Hidden Fortress</i> to outer space (<i>Star Wars</i>), or <i>Yojimbo</i> to the American West (<i>A Fist Full of Dollars</i>), but that doesn't negate the utility of feudal Japan, outer space, or the American West as distinct settings. You can set pretty much any kind of story anywhere, but the Directions have aesthetic and thematic strengths you can choose to play to or play against, and their flexibility doesn't render them redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T14:18:12-08:00","id":1502710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502702#post1502702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a trick.</div> </div> </div> </div> 50/50 that it is; Jenthreads tend to hyperbole to drive engagement, and it always, always works.<br /> <br /> We're on to you, <i>Jen</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T09:02:41-08:00","id":1503037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502710#post1502710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 50/50 that it is; Jenthreads tend to hyperbole to drive engagement, and it always, always works.<br /> <br /> We're on to you, <i>Jen</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not a bait thread I swear! Since I would like to write some travel guide to the four directions so they would need some hype on why you would like to visit them, but I feel like they are all kind samey on what kind of activities you can do, just with a different coat of paint.<br /> <br /> Though it seems that I can have the people reacts differently to a thing/activity like all the ruin examples here so each different will feels more unique, like Southern ruins tends to also be (partly) habitatable so you can visit Gem and a pyramid next door, while Northern ruins are all desolated places in the middle of nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:51:15-08:00","id":1503301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502518#post1502518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Environmentally linked settlement abandonments have historically been an outlier and I assume wyld zones and shadowlands wouldn't change that too drastically.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess if you're trying to factor the environmental impact of the Great Contagion killing 90% of all plant life, but I don't think that's being retained based on previous comments by developers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, if there are folks living nearby, significant ruins don't tend to last long - they get dismantled and hauled off to become building materials for the modern settlement, <i>or</i> they get settled <i>in</i> and then it's not so much &quot;ruins&quot; as &quot;new buildings that reuse old walls&quot; or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T23:37:00-08:00","id":1503307,"title":"","content":"Though if it got death traps like those ones in Nexus then they may stay untouched for quite a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T02:30:50-08:00","id":1503309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1503301#post1503301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, if there are folks living nearby, significant ruins don't tend to last long - they get dismantled and hauled off to become building materials for the modern settlement,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends on how nearby &quot;nearby&quot; is and how easy these structures are to take apart but yes, many ruins have been destroyed by people who didn't appreciate their value.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1503301#post1503301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>or</i> they get settled <i>in</i> and then it's not so much &quot;ruins&quot; as &quot;new buildings that reuse old walls&quot; or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends whose talking and in what context. If the old walls are a point of interest it's not unreasonable to describe them as ruins despite the fact they've now been incorporated into a new structure, but obviously someone wouldn't describe their house as a ruin for having an old wall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-17-2023, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T07:43:06-08:00","id":1504424,"title":"","content":"To Jen: I think you can emphasize ruins of specific places, activities like skiing, dog-sledding, riding animals unique the region, local cuisine and alcohol and drugs, local music, local festivals, seasonal flowers or autumn colors, and local entertainments like a theatre or a &quot;tame&quot; Fey who does shows. Even for seemingly similar activities like sailing, the actual visceral experience will vary a lot - consider local wind conditions, seasonality and severity of storms, the smell and sounds of saltwater vs. freshwater vs. a sandy desert, speed of water currents vs. none in a desert or on ice. Medical tourism might even be a thing, if there is some local medical herb or knowledge that costs more to import than to go visit, although I'm not sure if that makes sense in Creation.<br /> <br /> Also, the different environments do different things to ruins. In the East and other forest areas, they'll be overgrown unless someone has rediscovered and excavated them. In the West and coastal areas, they may be underwater. In the South they may be exposed, or partly buried in sand, or partly eroded by sand, but still -- more visible. In the North they are more likely to be exposed, but may be eroded or else covered by new glaciers. So, ruins in different regions won't be equally accessible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1502203-is-it-a-good-thing-you-can-do-gay-death-rival-tragedy-story-in-every-directions?p=1502518#post1502518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Environmentally linked settlement abandonments have historically been an outlier and I assume wyld zones and shadowlands wouldn't change that too drastically.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess if you're trying to factor the environmental impact of the Great Contagion killing 90% of all plant life, but I don't think that's being retained based on previous comments by developers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Isator Levi here. In the real world you're right, but the twin apocalypses have changed things:<br /> <br /> 1. The most densely populated places may be the most likely to become shadowlands in the Great Contagion.<br /> <br /> 2. The Contagion and Balorian Crusade both probably shifted dragon lines in many places, which could cause dangerous lingering magic, malfunctioning manses, Wyld Zones, or just places that are less habitable because the river shifted 3 miles to a different bed. Plus, 40% of Creation dissolved and the outer poles moved inwards, which would drastically change the environment near the new edges. The far North is just colder than before, the far South is drier and hotter, the far East more overgrown, etc.<br /> <br /> 3. The population collapsed. I don't think there are enough humans left in Creation to inhabit all the habitable ruins, even after 760+ years of population recovery.<br /> <br /> 4. Gods and elementals that once maintained nice living conditions may have gone rogue, died, been reassigned or Wyld-crazed, or released from bindings. Sorcery or artifice that made a location livable may have broken down or gone haywire.<br /> <br /> 5. Some trade routes have probably disappeared or shifted to very different routes, due to the above and to the generally &quot;lesser&quot; civilization. If the Guild hasn't reopened a given trade route, settlements that once relied on global connections may be unable to sustain themselves anymore. If the trade route has been reopened, maybe people started a new settlement 2 miles away from the lost, forgotten ruins of the older town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 03-05-2023, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T11:36:12-08:00","id":1504471,"title":"","content":"Uhhhhhg my post triggered the spam overreaction so I can't edit.<br /> <br /> I wanted to add that you can also think about local public artworks or monuments in inhabited places. Murals, carvings, sculptures, the walls of Medo, gardens, gorgeous temples and palaces. There may be spectacles staged by local rulers to legitimate their rule by impressing their subjects. Also consider natural wonders: waterfalls, geysers, volcanoes, rare or gigantic or miniature plants and animals, unusual mountains or kopjes or stones like Uluru, canyons, stone arches, etc. Consider animal migrations that may be spectacular: queleas, passenger pigeons, bison, caribou, mammoths, wild yeddim, monarch butterflies, colorful birds, seabirds, etc.<br /> <br /> Think about what pilgrims travelled for in pre-industrial periods: i.e. religious pilgrimage, but also springs (or people) with reputed healing powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":".  had another idea 03-05-2023, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}